cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite or quote these CV variants, please cite them as below."
title: "CV variants - one person, role-targeted packagings of a single resume record"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/cv"
url: "https://tonydzi.github.io/resume.json"
abstract: >-
  Role-targeted CV variants generated from one master record published as resume.json.
  Each markdown file packages the same career facts for a different role cluster -
  forward-deployed and solutions engineering, developer relations, technical product
  management and founding GTM, business development and partnerships, applied AI agent
  security, technical writing and AI education, stablecoin and digital-currency strategy,
  and exchange and trading infrastructure - by reordering and foregrounding, not by
  changing the history. The variants are emphasis rather than separate records, so they
  are not to be merged or summed; where a variant and the master record disagree, the
  master record governs. Self-reported career documents, published openly next to the
  author's open-source repositories so that technical claims can be checked against code
  rather than taken from the document.
keywords:
  - curriculum-vitae
  - resume
  - json-resume
  - career-documents
